<p>Explain the constructible universe <m>L</m> conceptually.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Explain forcing conceptually without technical construction.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Explain why forcing is useful for independence proofs.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Explain what a large-cardinal axiom is conceptually.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Explain why large cardinals are viewed as stronger existence principles.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study the derivation of the empty set from other standard ZF axioms.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Formalize each ZF axiom in first-order logic.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study the precise logical form of the Separation Schema.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study the precise logical form of the Replacement Schema.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove the recursion theorem on <m>\omega</m>.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Develop ordinal addition recursively.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Develop ordinal multiplication recursively.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Develop ordinal exponentiation recursively.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove transfinite induction.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study the transfinite recursion theorem.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study cardinal numbers as initial ordinals.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove the Cantor--Bernstein theorem.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study cardinal arithmetic with and without Choice.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove equivalence of the Axiom of Choice and the Well-Ordering Theorem.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove equivalence of Zorn's Lemma and the Axiom of Choice.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study the Ultrafilter Lemma and compare its strength with full Choice.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Develop the rank function rigorously.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove that every set belongs to some <m>V_\alpha</m>.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study transitive models of set theory.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study Gödel's constructible universe <m>L</m>.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study Cohen forcing conceptually.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study the independence of CH.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study inaccessible cardinals.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study measurable cardinals.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
